    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "SAFETY\nINFORMATION\nDC-8 jet\nmainliner\nUNITED",
      "*\nUNITED\nAIR LINES\nDOM-FO-422-200M-4/60\nPrinted in U.S.A.",
      "HOW TO OPEN DOOR EXITS\nEXIT\nThe four door exits all open in the same man-\nner. (1) Lift door handle as indicated, door will\nmove inward slightly.\n(2) Push door outward\nuntil it swings clear of door opening.\nHOW TO OPEN WINDOW EXITS\nEmergency window exits are located over wings.\n(1) Grasp handle as indicated and pull inward.\nEntire window unit is then discarded. (2) Pull\nout tapes from top of window casing to aid\ndescent from wing.\nFORWARD CABIN\nDOOR Y\nFORWARD GALLEY\nDOOR\nEMERGENCY\nSLIDE\nEMERGENCY\nSLIDE\nWINDOW EXITS\nWINDOW EXITS\nWINDOW TAPES\nTO AID DESCENT\nFROM WING\nWINDOW TAPES\n- то\nAID DESCENT\nFROM WING\nAFT GALLEY\nDOOR\nAFT CABIN\nDOOR\nEMERGENCY\nSLIDES\nHOW TO OPERATE EMERGENCY GROUND SLIDE\nI. OPEN EXIT DOOR FIRST\nESCAPE SLIDE 2. PULL OFF THIS COVER\nAfter door is open, pull off cover plate and discard.\nEmergency slide is packed into ceiling compartment\nimmediately in front of doors.\nGrasp bars as indicated and pull. This action un-\nlocks ceiling compartment.\nMaintain grasp on bar as ceiling panel door opens\nand slide packet drops to floor. A push will drop slide\nout cabin door.\nPlace bar under retainer hooks located on either side\nof the door at cabin floor level.\nTo inflate slide pull cord-tab hanging from valve on\nair hose about shoulder height as indicated.\nWhen using slides it is important that ladies remove\nhigh heels to avoid puncturing slide. The correct pro-\ncedure is to sit in slide as illustrated."
    ],
